      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 24,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Read me",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## SameFace, step by step\n\nA family photo (Library of Congress, public domain) edited onto a museum\nbackdrop, and one person in it measured and repaired.\n\n**Try it:** copy the two pictures in `custom_nodes/comfyui-sameface/example_workflows/input/` into `ComfyUI/input/`, or drag each onto its Load Image, then run. The models download on the first run, about 1.8 GB.\n\n- **Face Mask** chooses the person: the heads are counted left to right, and\n  index 1 is the mother. Use the same person on every side.\n- **Measure: the edit** measures her head, **Repair** moves it back, and\n  **Measure: the repair** measures what is left. Each has a slider, a shift\n  map and a histogram; the reports are in the Preview Any nodes.\n- Every setting is described in the pack's `docs/nodes.md`.\n\n**A slider is blank?** The built-in Compare Images needs **Modern Node Design (Nodes 2.0)** on: Settings \u2192 Comfy \u2192 Nodes 2.0. Or use **Image Comparer (rgthree)** in its place.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
  ],
